    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d295">

                <pb facs="0480" n="166" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/324</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-11T17:00:00+08:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 11, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</p>
                <p>Japanese Chargé d’Affaires reliably quoted as stating that his Government would
                    welcome an opportunity to participate in taking Kiaochow and that an expedition
                    for that purpose is available immediately. . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
